 288: #  ---- CLASS CLOSURE on the latch-collision axis: every other bit set FIRST, then the colour decline -----
 289: #  sgi_re_width_probe.py's `tex xbit' row proved this priming sequence fires bits 0-10 (bits 0-5 by a byte
 290: #  store to each RE window; 6 a byte store to the DE window; 7/8 a store to and a load from the straggler
 291: #  offset 0x1800; 9 an unimplemented drawing op; 10 a LIN_B rectangle) and its `tex rd lat1' row that a
 292: #  64-bit read of CRIME_RE_TEX fires bit 11.  With bits 0-11 all set, a BADCOLOR latch that SHARES any of
 293: #  them is already silenced when the YCRCB PUT arrives and `allbits announce' reads 0.  `allbits primed'
 294: #  counts the twelve priming announces so a priming access that silently stops firing reds the row
 295: #  instead of leaving a hole (the width probe's own repair for the same vacuity).  One session; the
 296: #  paint row is the decline control.  Added on the pass-2 repair chain at codex's finding.
 297: A = Addr(CODE)
 298: RE_WINDOWS = (0xb5001000, 0xb5001200, 0xb5001400, 0xb5001600, 0xb5001700, 0xb5001780)  # TLB_A..LINEAR_B
 299: DE_BASE   = 0xb5002000            # DEVICE_ACCESS(sgi_de): a byte access fires SGIRE_W_DE_LEN
 300: OUTSIDE   = 0xb5001800            # past LINEAR_B: the straggler arm (UNMAP_WR / UNMAP_RD)
 301: PRIM_BAD  = 0x05020000            # an UNIMPLEMENTED drawing op (only LINE and RECTANGLE exist)
 302: TEX_BASE  = 0xb5001600
 303: prime = []
 304: for _w in RE_WINDOWS:
 305:     prime += store(A, _w, 0x1, op=OP_SB_T0_A3)             # bits 0-5
 306: prime += store(A, DE_BASE, 0x1, op=OP_SB_T0_A3)            # bit 6
 307: prime += store(A, OUTSIDE, 0x1, op=OP_SB_T0_A3)            # bit 7
 308: prime += loadop(A, OUTSIDE, OP_LW_V0_AT)                   # bit 8
 309: prime += setup_put(A, MODE_LINB_RGBA)                      # bit 10 (a real 1x1 rectangle into LIN_B)
 310: prime += store(A, DE_PRIM_START, PRIM_BAD)                 # bit 9
 311: prime += loadop(A, TEX_BASE, OP_LD_V0_AT)                  # bit 11
